<Layout title="Resume | AJ Ranzato">
  <div class="resume">
    <header class="resume-header">
      <h1>Academic and Professional Experience</h1>
    </header>
    <!-- Experience goes here -->
    <section>
      <h2>Professional Experience</h2>

      <div class="resume-entry">
        <div class="resume-title">
          <h3>
            Field Interviewer,<strong
              >NYC Housing Preservation & Development</strong
            >
          </h3>
          <span class="date">2026–Present</span>
        </div>

        <p class="resume-subtitle">
          <em>New York City Housing &amp; Vacancy Survey</em>
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            Conduct in-person interviews across the city for the New York City
            Housing and Vacancy Survey (NYCHVS).
          </li>
          <li>
            Recruit and interview sampled units supporting city-wide data
            collection effort for enhanced policy decisions with regard to
            housing, affordability, neighborhood and building conditions.
          </li>
          <li>
            Engage directly with New Yorkers of various backgrounds encouraging
            civic participation with a friendly and professional demeanor.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="resume-entry">
        <div class="resume-title">
          <h3>Research Assistant, <strong>Village Preservation</strong></h3>
          <span class="date">2026–Present</span>
        </div>

        <p class="resume-subtitle">
          <em
            >Village Preservation works to document, celebrate, and preserve the
            architectural and cultural heritage of Greenwich Village, the East
            Village, and NoHo in New York City.</em
          >
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            Contributing to a longitudinal study of twenty years of commercial
            change along the Bleecker Street corridor in Greenwich Village.
          </li>
          <li>
            Developing a research-backed analysis of why the corridor's mix of
            independent businesses and national chains differs from comparable
            New York City commercial districts.
          </li>
          <li>
            Building longitudinal datasets documenting commercial continuity,
            displacement, and neighborhood change.
          </li>
          <li>
            Identifying trends in the evolving commercial character of the
            district.
          </li>
          <li>
            Conducting interviews with current and former business owners.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="resume-entry">
        <div class="resume-title">
          <h3>Senior Marketing Professional</h3>
          <span class="date">2015–2025</span>
        </div>

        <ul>
          <li>
